cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite this specification or kit, please cite it as below, and name the spec version and track you used."
type: software
title: "Open Mainframe Benchmark: specification and kit"
abstract: >-
  An open, reproducible benchmark specification, with a kit in development, for comparing IBM Z / LinuxONE with x86
  servers on online transactions and batch together, from the same source on every platform, with pre-registered
  hypotheses and a Full Disclosure Report for every result. Not a project of the Open Mainframe Project or The
  Linux Foundation, and not affiliated with either.
authors:
  - family-names: Mayne
    given-names: Andrew
    affiliation: "Durham College"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DrewMayne/open-mainframe-benchmark"
version: "0.4.0-draft"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - IBM Z
  - LinuxONE
  - x86
  - COBOL
  - CICS
  - reproducibility
  - pre-registration
